WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920 align:start position:19%
Today I'm going to share some tips and
techniques for creating vintage badge

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:09.599 align:start position:19%
logos. This popular design style is
based on the way brand identities were

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.679 align:start position:19%
created in previous centuries with
handlettered layouts that clearly

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:18.720 align:start position:19%
describe the company, unlike modern logo
designs of today that are condensed into

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:22.880 align:start position:19%
a simple icon graphic. I'll show you how
Illustrator's vector tools can help you

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:27.119 align:start position:19%
create interesting vintage style logos,
combining text effects and shapes to

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.439 align:start position:19%
build the layout. My artwork will be
based on a fictional 19th century denim

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:35.440 align:start position:19%
workware brand called Hamilton's.
Similar to the early days of Levis's or

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:39.760 align:start position:19%
Carheart, but this vintage style has
become popular for all kinds of logos,

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.600 align:start position:19%
packaging, and t-shirt designs. With
vintage style designs relying so heavily

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.480 align:start position:19%
on wording rather than imagery, it's
important to use fonts that

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.000 align:start position:19%
authentically replicate old hand
lettering. I'm using the Milktore

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:54.239 align:start position:19%
collection of fonts by my friends at
Heritage Typco. This all-in-one kit not

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:58.320 align:start position:19%
only includes five fonts with an
authentic handcrafted look that

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:03.199 align:start position:19%
perfectly complement each other, it also
provides 18 ready-made logo templates,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.960 align:start position:19%
over 30 vector graphics, and a series of
textures to add the finishing touch to

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:10.960 align:start position:19%
your work. It contains everything you
need to create vintage style logos,

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:15.520 align:start position:19%
badges, labels, packaging or title
designs with a handcrafted vibe. I've

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.520 align:start position:19%
teamed up with Heritage Type Co to offer
Spoon Graphics subscribers 10% off.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.759 align:start position:19%
Follow the link in the description and
use the code spoon of milk 20 during

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.799 align:start position:19%
checkout to secure the best price around
to create your vintage badge logo.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:33.360 align:start position:19%
Create a new document in Adobe
Illustrator. The artboard can be any

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:38.000 align:start position:19%
size. I prefer to then go to view and
hide artboards to give myself plenty of

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.920 align:start position:19%
space to work with.
Begin laying out the name of your brand

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.320 align:start position:19%
with a type tool. The Milktore font
collection contains five perfectly

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:50.720 align:start position:19%
pairing type faces. Number one is a
lovely brush script. Each font is also

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:55.040 align:start position:19%
supplied in clean, rough, and textured
variants. Use the basic clean version,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.920 align:start position:19%
and stick around till the end and I'll
show you an easy way to add extra

00:01:56.479 --> 00:02:01.439 align:start position:19%
roughness and texturing effects
separately.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.200 align:start position:19%
These prograde fonts are also packed
full of alternate and stylistic

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:09.200 align:start position:19%
characters. Place the cursor at the end
of the word, then open the glyphs panel.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:13.760 align:start position:19%
Test out the various swooshes and
swashes to find an underline that suits

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:18.480 align:start position:19%
your wording. This single piece of text
already looks like hand lettering rather

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:22.400 align:start position:19%
than being typed out using a font.
To further customize the text, click the

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:28.560 align:start position:19%
little envelope distort icon in the top
toolbar. Choose the rise option and set

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:32.879 align:start position:19%
the bend value to 20%.
Use the type tool to add some additional

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:37.360 align:start position:19%
text to the logo layout. This time, use
one of the other font styles.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.200 align:start position:19%
Set the center paragraph style and
adjust the character size and line

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:45.120 align:start position:19%
height values to set up the text. Then
make any necessary kerning adjustments

00:02:42.959 --> 00:02:48.879 align:start position:19%
by placing the cursor and using the left
and right keyboard keys while holding

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.959 align:start position:19%
Alt to adjust the individual letter
spacing.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.360 align:start position:19%
Add an arc effect to this text using the
same 20% bend.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.519 align:start position:19%
Align the two text elements up
centrally.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:05.200 align:start position:19%
Add more text elements, this time using
a different font. This collection makes

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:08.879 align:start position:19%
it easy to match font styles without
needing to find or buy additional

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.959 align:start position:19%
styles.
This time, let's decorate the text with

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:16.800 align:start position:19%
a shape element. Draw a rectangle to
surround the text. Then, right click and

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.560 align:start position:19%
choose arrange center back to place it
underneath the text.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:25.760 align:start position:19%
Change the text to white to make it
visible against the black rectangle.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:29.360 align:start position:19%
Select both elements and align them up.
The comma in this wording offsets the

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:34.400 align:start position:19%
vertical alignment slightly so it's
nudged into place optically.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.239 align:start position:19%
Envelope distort effects can still be
added to combinations of text and shapes

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.560 align:start position:19%
even though the icon is no longer there
in the top toolbar. Instead, go to

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:47.760 align:start position:19%
object, envelope distort, and make with
warp. This time, try out the flag

00:03:44.959 --> 00:03:51.599 align:start position:19%
effect.
Add more text elements elsewhere on the

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:56.799 align:start position:19%
artboard. We'll fit this wording inside
a diamond shape. So, draw a square, then

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:02.159 align:start position:19%
rotate it by 45°.
Go to object, transform, and scale.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:06.159 align:start position:19%
Check non-uniform and enter 300% for the
horizontal value.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.640 align:start position:19%
Place the diamond on top of the text and
go to object envelope distort make with

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:14.879 align:start position:19%
top object. But notice how the text is
being warped out of shape too much. Undo

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.199 align:start position:19%
the effect. Then make a copy of the
diamond shape to save it for later.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:23.520 align:start position:19%
Use the rectangle tool to draw a
straight edge covering the point of the

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:27.199 align:start position:19%
diamond. Alt and drag a copy to the
other side. Then shift and click to

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:31.280 align:start position:19%
select them both. Make a compound path
via the right click menu.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:35.520 align:start position:19%
Add the diamond to the selection and
center up the shapes. Then click the

00:04:33.759 --> 00:04:39.440 align:start position:19%
minus front button from the pathfinder
panel to punch out the shapes, leaving

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.360 align:start position:19%
two straight edges on either side of the
diamond. Repeat the envelope distort

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:47.160 align:start position:19%
effect and notice the text fits
perfectly into the shape.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:53.600 align:start position:19%
Go to edit and paste in back to replace
the original diamond shape we copied to

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:57.600 align:start position:19%
the clipboard. Currently the text is
black on black. So, right click and

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:01.919 align:start position:19%
choose isolate selected group to adjust
the original text element. Give it a

00:04:59.759 --> 00:05:05.360 align:start position:19%
white fill.
Exit back out to the top layer by

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:09.520 align:start position:19%
clicking the arrow icon in the top left
corner of the screen. Increase the

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:13.520 align:start position:19%
border around the text by adding a black
stroke to the diamond shape. Set the

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:17.759 align:start position:19%
alignment to outside. Then adjust the
size to suit.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:23.199 align:start position:19%
A little star graphic makes a nice
detail. Set it up with a white fill and

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:27.520 align:start position:19%
no stroke. Then move it into place.
Alt and drag a copy to the other side

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:31.280 align:start position:19%
and group them.
Hold shift and add the diamond to the

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:35.199 align:start position:19%
selection. Then give it an extra click
to make it the key object so it doesn't

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:39.840 align:start position:19%
move out of place.
Align the shapes up so they sit

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:43.120 align:start position:19%
perfectly centrally.
Group all the objects that make up this

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.160 align:start position:19%
piece of text. Then scale and position
it within the logo layout.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:53.600 align:start position:19%
Vintage logos can be layouts of text or
contained within outlining shapes. Let's

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.120 align:start position:19%
make this design a circular badge by
drawing a circle around the design,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.479 align:start position:19%
overlapping each end of the script
slightly.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:04.560 align:start position:19%
Give this circle a black stroke with an
appropriate weight.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:09.440 align:start position:19%
Find the scissors tool, then snip the
path and delete the unwanted portions

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:12.880 align:start position:19%
that overlap the script text.
Draw another circle that's slightly

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:17.199 align:start position:19%
larger. Clear it stroke, leaving an
invisible path. Select the type on a

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:20.400 align:start position:19%
path tool and click to type around the
circle.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:25.199 align:start position:19%
Add some more wording to the design in
one of the milk store fonts.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:29.600 align:start position:19%
Center it up at the top by dragging the
little alignment widget with the direct

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:33.039 align:start position:19%
selection tool.
Altering a font's tracking value to

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:36.639 align:start position:19%
space out the letters is a great way to
fill up the available area without

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:40.479 align:start position:19%
having to make the actual text size too
big.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:46.639 align:start position:19%
Copy and paste in front a duplicate of
this type on a path shape. Then edit the

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:50.160 align:start position:19%
wording. Rotate the circle by 180° to
place the text on the bottom. Then

00:06:48.639 --> 00:06:54.479 align:start position:19%
adjust the alignment handle with the
direct selection tool to place the text

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:59.120 align:start position:19%
the right way up.
While the text is now readable, it's set

00:06:56.479 --> 00:07:05.960 align:start position:19%
to the inside of the path. An easy fix
is to adjust the baseline shift value to

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:05.960 align:start position:19%
offset it to the outside of the path.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:12.160 align:start position:19%
Draw another circle to outline the
design. A trick to line it up centrally

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:16.960 align:start position:19%
is to turn on outline mode from the view
menu or the command and Y shortcut.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:21.560 align:start position:19%
Alt and drag the shape from the center
point. Then turn off outline mode again.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:30.319 align:start position:19%
Copy and paste this outlining circle to
add another slightly larger border. This

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:34.000 align:start position:19%
time with a much broader stroke.
As one last finishing touch, add another

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:38.720 align:start position:19%
star graphic to fill out the empty
space. This portion of the layout is

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:42.319 align:start position:19%
part of the type on a path area. So,
rotate the star to follow the circular

00:07:40.479 --> 00:07:46.560 align:start position:19%
outline.
Select the rotate tool, then turn on

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:50.880 align:start position:19%
outline mode. Click the center point,
then alt and drag a duplicate star. The

00:07:49.039 --> 00:07:55.440 align:start position:19%
pivot point will follow the rotation to
keep the star lined up perfectly. Use

00:07:53.360 --> 00:08:00.160 align:start position:19%
the command and D shortcut or control
and D on Windows to repeat the step one

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:04.400 align:start position:19%
more time to create three stars.
Select all three then go to object

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:08.080 align:start position:19%
transform and reflect. Hit copy to
generate a flipped set for the other

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:11.680 align:start position:19%
side.
Make any adjustments to the logo layout

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:16.319 align:start position:19%
and draw a selection across everything
and drag a duplicate off to one side.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:19.840 align:start position:19%
We'll keep a live backup. We process the
duplicate to permanently apply all the

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.840 align:start position:19%
effects and turn it into a completely
vector outline. To prevent the original

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:28.560 align:start position:19%
objects from being selected, go to
object lock selection. Then turn back on

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:32.800 align:start position:19%
the view artboards option so the design
is seen against the gray backdrop.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:37.279 align:start position:19%
Draw a selection around the duplicate.
Then go to object and expand appearance

00:08:35.039 --> 00:08:40.320 align:start position:19%
followed by objects and expand to apply
all the envelope distort effects and

00:08:38.959 --> 00:08:43.760 align:start position:19%
convert the text and strokes to
outlines.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:49.839 align:start position:19%
Ungroup the objects. Then select a black
filled element. Go to select same and

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:54.560 align:start position:19%
fill color. Merge all these shapes into
one outline by clicking the unite option

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:59.040 align:start position:19%
in the pathfinder panel. Also turn it
into a compound path under the object

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:03.440 align:start position:19%
compound path and make menu. This is
required for an upcoming step to ensure

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:06.959 align:start position:19%
the pathfinder tool works correctly.
Right click and choose arrange center

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:11.360 align:start position:19%
back to make the white elements visible.
Then repeat the process for these

00:09:08.399 --> 00:09:16.720 align:start position:19%
objects. Select same filler color unite.
Make a compound path.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.560 align:start position:19%
Add the black objects to the selection
along with the white objects. Then click

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:25.279 align:start position:19%
the minus front button in the pathfinder
panel to punch out the shapes leaving a

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:28.880 align:start position:19%
continuous outline.
There's an easy way to add some cool

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.880 align:start position:19%
texturing effects to your vintage logo.
That's by downloading my free ink stamp

00:09:30.959 --> 00:09:37.120 align:start position:19%
texturizer from Spoon Graphics by
following the link in the description.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:41.519 align:start position:19%
Double click the smart objects layer and
paste in your logo to replace the

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:46.000 align:start position:19%
placeholder. Save and close the PSB to
find your logo processed with cool ink

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:49.519 align:start position:19%
bleed and texturing effects.
You can change the color if necessary or

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:53.360 align:start position:19%
play with the texturing options to find
the best spread of details.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:57.200 align:start position:19%
If you want to learn how to create these
effects yourself, check out my video

00:09:55.200 --> 00:10:02.080 align:start position:19%
titled How to Create a Distressed Letter
Press Print Effect in Photoshop.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.920 align:start position:19%
The final result is a vintage logo with
a neat layout of text elements, all

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:10.240 align:start position:19%
contained within a circular outline to
create a badge style brand design. The

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:15.120 align:start position:19%
Milk Store font collection made font
pairing easy with the five expertly

00:10:12.399 --> 00:10:18.240 align:start position:19%
designed type faces included in one kit.
Then with the help of a few of

00:10:16.399 --> 00:10:22.800 align:start position:19%
Illustrator's tools and effects, it's
all combined into an authenticl looking

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:27.120 align:start position:19%
vintage logo design. If you enjoyed this
tutorial or learned new tips and tricks,

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:31.279 align:start position:19%
a thumbs up on the video would be really
appreciated. Stick around for more of my

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.959 align:start position:19%
content by subscribing to the channel
and be sure to join my mailing list at

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:38.880 align:start position:19%
Spoon Graphics to download all my free
design resources. As always, thank you

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:42.360 align:start position:19%
very much for watching and I'll see you
in the next one.

